  "_comment": "CRS policy areas as Congress.gov prints them, their catalog ids and the topic group each belongs to. The page shows eight groups (one colour each: eight is the most a categorical palette keeps distinguishable, so there is no 'Other topics'); the area stays on each law. Regroup by editing `group` here and re-running `pnpm transform`; nothing is re-fetched. 'Commemorations' is a CRS label applied only in 1985-88 and 1997-2008; it is its own group, and the transform also counts there any law whose title matches the rules in transform/laws-commemorative.ts (the CRS area stays on the law as crs_area_id). `legacy_terms` are subject terms older laws carry in the policy-area field; they count as 'Not classified' and are never mapped to an area by us. A name in neither list stops the transform. The legacy terms were listed from the raw files of the 93rd-107th Congresses (160 terms on 391 laws, all in the 93rd-95th); a term not listed stops the build.",
